# G0.3: one late import of a 4 GiB handoff (unexplained, not reproduced)
environment: simulator, iPhone 17, iOS 26.5 (Sylvia-M0-g03-intake), 2026-10-06
build: working tree between commits b91a8ff and 0464ef6 (64-bit share size fix in place; scan timing NOT yet logged)
command: xcodebuild test-without-building ... -only-testing:IntakeHarnessUITests/ShareSheetUITests/testExtensionMemoryDoesNotGrowWithFileSize

What happened: the extension received the full 4,294,967,297 bytes and showed "Received", but the harness's job count
did not rise within the test's 120 s wait, and the test case took 335 s in all. Inspecting the simulator containers
afterwards: the App Group inbox was empty, the handoff was in Staging/Staged, and the journal's job for it had
createdAt 2026-10-06T02:11:18Z, about 5 minutes after the 4 GiB share file was created (15:06 local = 02:06Z).
The bytes were intact and imported once; nothing was imported early or twice. Why the scan ran late is unknown:
that build did not log when scans were requested or how long they ran.

After this run the harness logs every scan (trigger, request time, wait, duration). In every later run (one by
hand, two CI trials and the clean CI run) every share was imported by the "after share" scan. In the clean run
(sim-app-tests.log) that scan was requested 0.70-0.76 s after Done was tapped, started without waiting, and ran
1.5 s for the 4 GiB + 1 handoff and 2.9 s for the 8 GiB + 1 handoff. Kept as an open item in the G0.3 report.

